# CXL: Compute Express Link memory -- pooling / expansion / hotplug.  A
# workload-host feature (not every metal image: a reclaim kernel doesn't want
# it), so it rides in the host profiles' OVERRIDES, not platform-metal.  PMEM
# mode omitted on purpose (needs LIBNVDIMM; Optane is EOL) -- this is volatile
# CXL.mem as NUMA capacity + devdax.  ZONE_DEVICE + memory hotplug support it.
CONFIG_MEMORY_HOTPLUG=y
CONFIG_MEMORY_HOTREMOVE=y
CONFIG_ZONE_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_CXL_BUS=y
CONFIG_CXL_PCI=y
CONFIG_CXL_ACPI=y
CONFIG_CXL_MEM=y
CONFIG_CXL_REGION=y

# The devdax half of the sentence above, which was missing entirely: CXL_REGION
# assembles the region, and with no DAX stack there is no device to hand out
# and no way to online it, so "+ devdax" was a claim the config could not meet.
#
#   DEV_DAX_CXL binds a volatile CXL region and publishes /dev/daxN.M -- the
#     devdax path itself, for a workload that wants the capacity mapped
#     directly rather than through the page allocator.
#   DEV_DAX_KMEM is how `daxctl reconvert-device --mode=system-ram` hot-adds
#     that same region as a memory-only NUMA node.  So it also carries the
#     "as NUMA capacity" half whenever capacity is assigned at RUNTIME (pooled
#     / hot-added CXL) rather than presented by firmware at boot -- which is
#     the case this fragment exists for.
#
# Every dependency is already satisfied on all four profiles that pull this
# fragment (hypervisor, hypervisor-dpu, gpu-node, trusted-compute) on both
# arches: DEV_DAX needs TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE (=y from the base), DEV_DAX_KMEM
# needs MEMORY_HOTPLUG and DEV_DAX_CXL needs CXL_BUS + CXL_REGION (all above),
# and the dax core maps its pages through ZONE_DEVICE (above).
#
# DEV_DAX_PMEM stays off on its own -- it depends on LIBNVDIMM, which is the
# thing the header says is deliberately absent.  FS_DAX is not wanted either:
# that is a filesystem mapped onto pmem, and this is volatile memory with no
# filesystem on it.  DEV_DAX_HMEM is NOT requested but will resolve =y anyway
# (it is `default DEV_DAX` and EFI_SOFT_RESERVE=y on both arches); recorded
# rather than stripped, because it claims EFI soft-reserved ranges that are
# not behind a CXL window, and with no driver those ranges are just stranded.
CONFIG_DAX=y
CONFIG_DEV_DAX=y
CONFIG_DEV_DAX_CXL=y
CONFIG_DEV_DAX_KMEM=y
# A CXL region nobody can address is the defect this block fixes; keep the
# header and the symbols from drifting apart again.
# ASSERT-ALL: CONFIG_CXL_REGION => CONFIG_DEV_DAX CONFIG_DEV_DAX_CXL CONFIG_DEV_DAX_KMEM
